35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Based on my research, I've noticed a clear trade-off. Last year, we were so independent that some of us barely saw each other. Conversely, in a shared house, there's almost no way to get a moment of true solitude.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very interesting point, Mizuki. It seems we must balance our togetherness with a little peace. I've found that all-in rates and whole-house rentals make the payments much simpler and fairer for everyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the inns have very strict mealtimes and we'd all sleep in one room. The island houses only have one bathroom, and some people said the water gets cold. I'm a bit worried about that.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings suggest a significant difference in travel. The city is effortless, but the island requires strict timing with the ferry, effectively consuming two full days. The spa valley is a middle ground, though the bus schedule is limited.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've found that the valley inn is quite predictable at 17,000 yen including meals. In contrast, the island houses are cheaper per night, but since food is extra, the final cost is harder to pin down.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Minato, the shared room at the inn might feel crowded, but @Jonathan's point about the island's travel time suggests we'd be forced together for days. We need a setting that allows us to be together without feeling trapped.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, since the island costs are harder to pin down, I worry someone might end up paying more than others. A whole-house rental or a fixed rate would be so much more peaceful for our hearts and wallets.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Mizuki, I think I would feel trapped if we all slept in one room. And @Jonathan, the island sounds like a long trip. I'm worried about the cold water and the strict times at the inn too.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I understand your concern. If the island consumes two days of our trip just for transit, it adds a layer of exhaustion before we even arrive. The city's flexibility seems far more restorative.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, I completely agree. The uncertainty of the island's food costs makes me uneasy. The valley inn's all-in rate is very appealing because we'd know exactly what to expect from the start.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we are torn between the predictability of the valley inn and the flexibility of the city. However, we must consider that the city allows for the natural solitude I found missing in shared houses.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mizuki, you make a fair point about solitude. However, if we choose the city, we must be careful that the separate bookings don't lead to unfair price differences like we had last time.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,I think the city sounds the best. Having a door and no strict timetable would make me feel much more relaxed. I don't want to worry about cold water or sleeping in one big room.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Minato. The city's effortless transit means we spend our time experiencing the destination rather than waiting for ferries or buses. It seems the most efficient way to ensure we all return home truly rested.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Minato, @Jonathan, I can see why the city is appealing for your comfort. However, I'm worried that separate bookings might lead to the same budget surprises we've had before. Can we ensure the costs are fixed?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Midori, we can agree on a budget cap or a specific hotel chain to keep costs consistent. The city offers the best balance: we can move as a group but still have the space to breathe.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very thoughtful suggestion, Mizuki. If we can find a way to keep the costs consistent, the city sounds like a wonderful choice that respects everyone's needs for both togetherness and peace.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm really happy we're thinking about this. If we can make sure the costs are fair, I think the city is the best place for us to be happy and relaxed.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. The city minimizes the logistical burden and eliminates the stress of strict schedules. If we can resolve the budget concerns, it is clearly the most restorative option for all of us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"If we can agree on a fixed budget cap or a specific hotel to avoid those surprises, I'm on board. I appreciate you all considering my concerns. Let's go with the city!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
